---
// Want a photo? Put it in src/assets/, import it, and add
// <Image src={portrait} alt="…" class="portrait" /> from 'astro:assets' before .text.
---

<section id="about" class="section" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="text">
      <span class="eyebrow">04 — About</span>
      <h2 id="about-title" class="visually-hidden">About me</h2>
      <p class="statement">
        The best data products answer the question you were about to ask.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Before I wrote a line of code, I spent six years as a claims adjuster at State Farm, turning
        messy information into decisions people had to live with. It turns out that's most of
        frontend work too. Since an apprenticeship in 2017, I've built reporting at Mailchimp,
        internal tools used by 30,000 people at Nationwide and customer portals for an insurtech
        startup. On my own time I'm designing Caldera, a money app that tells you what to do next,
        not just what already happened. Next, I want a software engineering role, frontend-focused, on a team
        building analytics, data or fintech products, in Atlanta or remote.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .split {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(20px, 5.5vw, 80px);
  }

  .portrait {
    width: 360px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .text {
    max-width: 760px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .statement {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.25rem + 1vw, 2.125rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .muted {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .split {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    .portrait {
      width: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    }
  }
</style>
